{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for reporting this. Your mailbox is healthy and well under its size limit, and your laptop is online and checking in normally. Since your phone is getting everything, the problem is most likely just Outlook on your laptop. Please try these steps in order and stop when new mail starts coming in:\n1. If you'd like to double-check, open Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com) and make sure your new mail shows there.\n2. In Outlook on your laptop, go to the Send / Receive tab and check whether 'Work Offline' is highlighted. If it is, click it to turn it off.\n3. Close Outlook completely, then open it again.\n4. Restart your laptop.\n5. If it's still stuck, we can rebuild your Outlook profile. Go to Control Panel > Mail > Show Profiles > Add, create a new profile, set it as the default, then open Outlook. Your mail will download again, which can take a little while.\nIf none of this works, or if your new mail is also missing from Outlook on the web, reply to this ticket and we'll pass it straight to our next-level team.",
  "internal_note": "Followed KB-009. lookup_user: account active, no lockouts, mailbox 17.4% used (8.9/50 GB), so KB-010 (mailbox full) doesn't apply. Device BL-LT-0101 is online, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:57 UTC, 60% disk free, no warnings. Mobile mail works, which suggests the mailbox and service are fine and the issue is in the desktop client. Sent the user the KB-009 self-service fix steps (Work Offline, restart Outlook and laptop, rebuild profile). Escalation criteria not met: one user, mailbox healthy. Note that the user is a VIP (CEO). If she replies that it's still broken, or that Outlook on the web is also missing mail, escalate to Tier 2 right away or offer a desk-side visit.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-009",
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
